---
title: Easy Vegan Falafel
portions: 12
category: Main
source: "https://minimalistbaker.com/easy-vegan-falafel/"
---

## Dough

[Blend] Add the @chickpeas{250 g}(drained), the @parsley{15 g}(chopped), the @shallot{100 g}(roughly chopped), the @garlic{12 g}(minced), the @sesame-seeds{18 g}, the @cumin{3 g}, the @coriander{1 g}, the @cardamom{0.5 g}, the @salt{1 g} and the @black pepper{} to a #food processor{}. Pulse to a crumbly dough — not a paste.

[Bind] Add the @flour{30 g} one tablespoon (~8 g) at a time, pulsing after each, until the dough holds together when molded into a ball without sticking.

[Chill] Transfer to a #mixing bowl{}, cover and refrigerate, ~{60 min}. This firms up the dough.

## Shape & fry

[Shape] Scoop rounded tablespoons (~30 g) and form into 11–12 small discs.

[Fry] Heat the @vegetable-oil{45 ml} in a large #skillet{} over medium heat. Fry the falafel in batches until deep golden brown on both sides, ~{5 min} total per batch. Drain on paper towels.

[Crisp] Optional: finish in a preheated ^{204°C} #oven{}, ~{8 min}, for extra crispiness.

## Serve

[Serve] Serve warm in pita bread with hummus and a garlic-herb sauce.
